{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition","id":1198170,"title":"Demon: The Fallen / Mummy 20th Anniversary Edition??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-21T17:20:44-07:00","id":1198170,"title":"Demon: The Fallen / Mummy 20th Anniversary Edition??","content":"So, at this point with 5th Edition due out later this year I think it's a safe to say we aren't getting anymore 20th Anniversary Editions, like for these two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23951-acwrig2","name":"acwrig2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T17:45:13-07:00","id":1198180,"title":"","content":"I sure hope that's not the case, particularly with Demon. It was always one of my favorite lines. It would have benefited so much from another edition, and I feel it gets such an unfair treatment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T17:47:02-07:00","id":1198181,"title":"","content":"<br /> Yeah I will be disappointed if we don't get Kindred of the East, Mummy, and Demon! And to a lesser extent hunter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T17:55:59-07:00","id":1198186,"title":"","content":"We don\u2019t know. <br /> <br /> Keep an eye on things in 2019 for Hunter20. If the KS for that materializes during that year, then yeah: Mummy20 and Demon20 will probably follow afterwards. If 2019 comes and goes with no Hunter20 KS, then yeah, no more WoD20. <br /> <br /> Me personally: I doubt nuWW wants to can EVERY WoD20 line. V20 and W20 ending right now makes sense (controversial views about Changing Ways aside) and has had a long and developed line. M20, Wr20, and C20 have barely started as game lines. It would make no sense to cancel them now. Plus, nuWW seems mostly interested in getting the 5th editions of the Big 3 out first. Everything else after that like Wraith, Changeling, Demon, etc? Probably not as high a priority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T18:33:48-07:00","id":1198200,"title":"","content":"I would be overjoyed ifnwe saw Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T19:12:37-07:00","id":1198205,"title":"","content":"I'd bet we'll get Hunter 20, but the others? Maybe Demon 20, maybe.<br /> <br /> Mummy and KOTE are probably pretty unlikely. (Mummy being a very small line and KOTE being....let's call it problematic and leave it at that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T19:57:19-07:00","id":1198216,"title":"","content":"I asked them about KotE20 on Twitter and they didn't give a promising answer. They also stated that not every WoD line is getting a 20th edition, and they apologized for it. So I'm not to optimistic about any of them, really. <br /> <br /> Martin seems in love with Vampire, Werewolf a close second, and Mage a distant third. I feel like the other lines are afterthoughts to him.<br /> <br /> But I HOPE I'm wrong...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T20:10:05-07:00","id":1198218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Novagain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1198205#post1198205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd bet we'll get Hunter 20, but the others? Maybe Demon 20, maybe.<br /> <br /> Mummy and KOTE are probably pretty unlikely. (Mummy being a very small line and KOTE being....let's call it problematic and leave it at that.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its sad but I would be soooo satisfied with a compiled and updated rules for Mummy and KOTE, even if they are Sublines. It would be great to have the high end powers for non Amenti Immortals. And KOTE is pre-revised rules so they are in desperate need of an update, and If their rules are updated to the quality of Changeling 20 or Dark Age Twenty I would love it! I want to finally play these updated!<br /> <br /> And oh man I want more Dark Ages stuff!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:14:14-07:00","id":1198525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1198218#post1198218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its sad but I would be soooo satisfied with a compiled and updated rules for Mummy and KOTE, even if they are Sublines. It would be great to have the high end powers for non Amenti Immortals. And KOTE is pre-revised rules so they are in desperate need of an update, and If their rules are updated to the quality of Changeling 20 or Dark Age Twenty I would love it! I want to finally play these updated!<br /> <br /> And oh man I want more Dark Ages stuff!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well KOTE was released as an option On ST vault so someone COULD make a revised updated version...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T12:43:44-07:00","id":1202685,"title":"","content":"I hope that we don't see anything from Demon: The Fallen ever again.<br /> <br /> As for KOTE, given the problems that whole line has, I'm surprised it even made it to the Storyteller's Vault at all.<br /> <br /> Mummy or Hunter 20th Anniversary Edition, I'd be fine with. Hell, I'd love to see a X20 version of Hunter: The Reckoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:04:31-07:00","id":1202753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1202685#post1202685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I hope that we don't see anything from Demon: The Fallen ever again.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Mummy or Hunter 20th Anniversary Edition, I'd be fine with. Hell, I'd love to see a X20 version of Hunter: The Reckoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with your last sentence, I don't understand how anyone could have the opinion of your first one(in bold). There are many Demon fans on this forum that would love a clean and tidy version of Demon 20; if it's something you're not interested in, don't buy it.<br /> <br /> I couldn't care less about Exalted, but I'm not about to start a crusade stating that I hope the Kickstarter fails. I hope, in the end, that people are happy. And as there are fans of Demon, I'd like to see a great 20th anniversary edition released that would make those fans happy.<br /> <br /> *shrugs<br /> <br /> You do you, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T05:34:22-07:00","id":1202955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1202753#post1202753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I agree with your last sentence, I don't understand how anyone could have the opinion of your first one(in bold). There are many Demon fans on this forum that would love a clean and tidy version of Demon 20; if it's something you're not interested in, don't buy it.<br /> <br /> I couldn't care less about Exalted, but I'm not about to start a crusade stating that I hope the Kickstarter fails. I hope, in the end, that people are happy. And as there are fans of Demon, I'd like to see a great 20th anniversary edition released that would make those fans happy.<br /> <br /> *shrugs<br /> <br /> You do you, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if there is a Demon 20, then I will just not buy it and pretend it didn't happen like I do with the first version of Demon: The Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:34:18-07:00","id":1203104,"title":"","content":"I'd like a D20 that cleaned up the mechanics, but it's nothing I haven't done on my own. It would just save me the hassle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","name":"thespiraleffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T16:36:29-07:00","id":1203177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1202955#post1202955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if there is a Demon 20, then I will just not buy it and pretend it didn't happen like I do with the first version of Demon: The Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok...not sure why you're making a big deal out of this.<br /> <br /> No one's forcing you to buy into a potential Demon20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T23:04:06-07:00","id":1203306,"title":"","content":"I think problematic elements speaks, in some ways, more for a 20th for Mummy, Demon or KotE. KotE in particular would benefit greatly for a better developed, better researched 20th anniversary, to say nothing of cleaning up it's mechanics. Demon never really had a chance so a 20th anniversary would potentially be practically a 2nd edition in all but name as beyond things like the problematic passages in the Earthbound book, the line desperately needed another edition to fix it's mechanical woes. Mummy was stillborn in some ways similar to Demon. It was a sub supplement line of Vampire for the vast majority of it's existence and Resurrection was the only real place it started to branch out from that. I've passed on from the WoD so I don't have any great anticipation for any of these potential titles but it would interesting to see none the less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T06:59:48-07:00","id":1203400,"title":"","content":"I really need Hunter 20 and D20 in my life. It's hard to mix editions without the update. I wish they'd give us a list of what they do and don't plan on making so I don't sit around waiting to buy the books I need in case they get updates. I don't wanna buy anything without a 20th after Hunter:tR needed revision to mesh with V20. At least if I don't have to that is. I also hate feeling pushed into the new edition. Literally not a single soul in my groups reacted well to V 5th pre-alpha. They begged me not to buy it when I told them I didn't like it either. I don't wanna deal with actual Gehenna nor do I like all the blood book keeping, the coin flip dice, or the dumbing down of attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23892-damienls","name":"DamienLS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23892_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T08:37:08-07:00","id":1203420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DamienLS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1203400#post1203400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really need Hunter 20 and D20 in my life. It's hard to mix editions without the update. I wish they'd give us a list of what they do and don't plan on making so I don't sit around waiting to buy the books I need in case they get updates. I don't wanna buy anything without a 20th after Hunter:tR needed revision to mesh with V20. At least if I don't have to that is. I also hate feeling pushed into the new edition. Literally not a single soul in my groups reacted well to V 5th pre-alpha. They begged me not to buy it when I told them I didn't like it either. I don't wanna deal with actual Gehenna nor do I like all the blood book keeping, the coin flip dice, or the dumbing down of attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, we did get Hunters Hunted 2. That's sort of like a 20th Anniversary edition of hunter. It's not the same as Reckoning, but hey better than nothing at all, like we have for Mummy, KOTE and Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23951-acwrig2","name":"acwrig2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T11:25:14-07:00","id":1203467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acwrig2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1203420#post1203420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, we did get Hunters Hunted 2. That's sort of like a 20th Anniversary edition of hunter. It's not the same as Reckoning, but hey better than nothing at all, like we have for Mummy, KOTE and Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just feel like they started 5th edition too early and that it was never meant for OWoD players. I hope they don't drop 4th edition. Also this may seem like a strange question, but I'm not too familiar with KotE, is it entirely standalone or does it mostly work off of vampire? It seems like if it's very much like VtM one could tweak it up to v20 standards more easily than some other games. I use revised clanbooks with V20 for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23892-damienls","name":"DamienLS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23892_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T12:20:29-07:00","id":1203482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DamienLS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1203467#post1203467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also this may seem like a strange question, but I'm not too familiar with KotE, is it entirely standalone or does it mostly work off of vampire? It seems like if it's very much like VtM one could tweak it up to v20 standards more easily than some other games. I use revised clanbooks with V20 for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is it's own stand-alone game.<br /> <br /> Haven't sat down to read the rules, but skimming over my PDF, I would say that...no, it wouldn't be as simple as just slapping the existing V20 rules and calling it a day. It does appear that KotE has it's own distinct sub-systems that porting V20's stuff wouldn't be a clean fit.<br /> <br /> And my impression is that OPP doesn't seem interested in pursuing a KotE20. Neither is nu-WW, since despite controversial statements and decisions, even THEY are hesitant at the idea of diving into a KotE5e.<br /> <br /> Or rather: &quot;We don't have enough Asian writers on staff to do the material culturally justice&quot; since a long-standing issue with WoD and Asia is the whole thing reeking of...pretty bad Orientalism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T16:03:08-07:00","id":1205000,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see 20th editions of them. I'd pay good money for them.<br /> <br /> I don't hold out much hope.<br /> <br /> Given the vast number of projects OPP has under it's belt right now, I feel burnout could easily be an issue; combined with the other factors (less popular lines, not the latest standard, the potential need to convince WW), I can see them being less of a prioity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:02:15-07:00","id":1205638,"title":"","content":"I'm a huge fan of Mummy: the Resurrection (not really in to the prior editions, which were bogged down with the whole &quot;boo-hoo, oh, my humanity&quot; shtick that was best kept in Vampire: the Masquerade), and while I wasn't fond of prior editions, I did mine them for more details for playing Shaunkhsen mummies (those with the Lesser Resurrection flaw) and for the spell components listed in 1st Edition, as inspiration to put more plot behind Hekau. Having the Reborn not be something cursed, doomed to utter and unavoidable failure, and actually making them a more positive thing was a refreshing thing that made the game so interesting. I've been holding out hope for 20th Anniversary Edition, and I definitely hope that when they roll out the 5th Edition WoD, that Mummy isn't either cast aside and forgotten or turned back in the direction of its lacking predecessors. <br /> I also really love Hunter: the Reckoning. I would similarly like to see it get a 20th Annviersary Edition treatment, and then a 5th Edition after that. With this being said, it's good that V20 gave us a Hunters' Hunted 2, as while it now falls under the Reckoning banner, those type of Hunters are best with their own rules, apart from those in Hunter: the Reckoning First Contact was needed, only because there was no Revised Edition version of those kind of hunters. Anything 20th Anniversary (or later) regarding Hunter: First Contact, could focus more on the story fluff, with the mechancis being contained to their own books (which did them more justice than First Contact did, although it did well with what it had). <br /> Regarding Demon, I thought that it was a great game, but it had the stench of writers, aware that the WoD was ending, trying to make it the be-all to explain everything, which it did poorly. While this scantly matters if you play in a game where the only game is Demon: the Fallen, we all know damned well that a great many games are crossover (and in My years of storytelling and playing, I don't view this as a negative thing - what can I say? I've seen it done well and have done it well), and that even in many demon-only games, you're going to get that storyteller that happens to appreciate the other games and would rather not just leave it with Demon's explanation. In this respect, while I love WoD and really dislike Chronicles of Darkness, I have to respect the greater effort of compatibility that was put into CoD (even if I utterly despise how they use a lack of a coherent backstory and claim that this is to avoid bogging people in metaplot, despite EXALTED having a VERY established history and NOT bogging down people in metaplot - I digress, as I am now ranting). A 20th Anniversary Edition (and later 5th edition) Demon: the Fallen book could do with just a few little changes, so that it doesn't feel like they're trying to make Gaia, the Judges of Ma'at, and a ton of other shit, like Charon, from Wraith, be explained as really being Fallen. (Maybe also deal with how TRUE FAITH works in the Demon setting and what the Fallen feel around such people.)<br /> Of course, there's also Wraith 20th Anniversary. This project really needs to be completed and made available, at long last. Hell! This book could see a lot of use, not only in Wraith games, but also Demon, Hunter, Mummy, Vampire, Mage, and Werewolf. Maybe Changeling? I don't know Changeling, so I'll leave that there. Sufficed to say, Wraith was and remains a beautiful game, and it deserves to see a 20th Anniversary Edition game (and then, in time, 5th Edition) become available. There are too many people that will never know the wonders of Shadow Guiding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:47:53-07:00","id":1205822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1205638#post1205638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, there's also Wraith 20th Anniversary. This project really needs to be completed and made available, at long last. Hell! This book could see a lot of use, not only in Wraith games, but also Demon, Hunter, Mummy, Vampire, Mage, and Werewolf. Maybe Changeling? I don't know Changeling, so I'll leave that there. Sufficed to say, Wraith was and remains a beautiful game, and it deserves to see a 20th Anniversary Edition game (and then, in time, 5th Edition) become available. There are too many people that will never know the wonders of Shadow Guiding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm...Wraith does have a 20th Anniversary version. In fact, the Backer PDF went out for that a few months ago. It's still going to be a bit before it's available for everyone, but it's closer to completion then it's ever been.<br /> <br /> And Changeling 20th Anniversary has been officially out for everyone for about a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T21:51:28-07:00","id":1205914,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm actually looking at my hard copy of C20 right now, and my pdf of Wr20 is open in Foxit as well.<br /> <br /> P.S. Charon from Wraith is never explained as one of the Fallen, that's a dire misread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T12:03:26-07:00","id":1206116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1205914#post1205914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm actually looking at my hard copy of C20 right now, and my pdf of Wr20 is open in Foxit as well.<br /> <br /> P.S. Charon from Wraith is never explained as one of the Fallen, that's a dire misread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the Author who wrote the Demon section explained he never intended the Wraith Charon to be the Demon, only to inherit the name as a sort of title. Nhudri on the other hand seems to be Nhudriel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T14:28:35-07:00","id":1206166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1205638#post1205638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Demon, I thought that it was a great game, but it had the stench of writers, aware that the WoD was ending, trying to make it the be-all to explain everything, which it did poorly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It only is a problem in the Storyteller doesn't like the idea of Creation coming first. WtA and Mage cosmologies fit perfectly after the Fallen marched into the Pit. You have to remember, there were infinite layers of reality prior that moment. Adam and Eve were the first man and woman, while on another level, billions of years of evolution produced the first human primates. The world existed as both physical and metaphysical and it wasn't until the War that these different realities began to slam together.<br /> <br /> One can easily flip it around and go with the standard WtA cosmology as being the end all be all. Demon can fit in it rather easy. It just takes a bit of plotting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1205638#post1205638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this respect, while I love WoD and really dislike Chronicles of Darkness, I have to respect the greater effort of compatibility that was put into CoD (even if I utterly despise how they use a lack of a coherent backstory and claim that this is to avoid bogging people in metaplot, despite EXALTED having a VERY established history and NOT bogging down people in metaplot - I digress, as I am now ranting).</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree. The lack of a foundation in the setting of CoD completely turns me off from much of the game. Unfortunately, it was an over reaction on the part of WW in response to critics of WoD's tangle metaplots. Maybe they knew there was no way to please everyone, so don't even bother. I think it was this thinking that lead them to take Descent in the direction it went.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1205638#post1205638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon: the Fallen book could do with just a few little changes, so that it doesn't feel like they're trying to make Gaia, the Judges of Ma'at, and a ton of other shit, like Charon, from Wraith, be explained as really being Fallen. (Maybe also deal with how TRUE FAITH works in the Demon setting and what the Fallen feel around such people.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia is an angel, not a Fallen. The Malhim were the first shifters. The Judges could be Ophanim, if we really wanted to go deep into the cosmology. If a Storyteller chooses Demon as the base for the metaplot, those are perfectly fine assumptions and do not undermine Werewolf. Or it can be flipped around. It's really up to the person running the game. Just because something is in a book doesn't mean it has to be followed. And as already pointed out, Charon the Halaku is not Charon the Wraith.<br /> <br /> As for True Faith, already taken care of. They have a faith potential of five. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","name":"thespiraleffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T16:03:56-07:00","id":1206186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thespiraleffect</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1206166#post1206166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. It only is a problem in the Storyteller doesn't like the idea of Creation coming first. WtA and Mage cosmologies fit perfectly after the Fallen marched into the Pit. You have to remember, there were infinite layers of reality prior that moment. Adam and Eve were the first man and woman, while on another level, billions of years of evolution produced the first human primates. The world existed as both physical and metaphysical and it wasn't until the War that these different realities began to slam together.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of failed attempts to sell people on the Wyld as an interesting place in Exalted. Is it a seething, infinite space of limitless chaos that can allow for anything? Well, yes, but it also often gets presented without structure, making all the hype so much hot air. It ultimately means nothing and has no draw of note compared to the rich tapestry of drama and weirdness that you get inside Creation. So, too, does the &quot;layers of reality&quot; explanation fail to produce any form of significant heat; it's a meaningless buzzword that amounts to the same mutual incompatibility that all the other games have for each other when playing to their own themes. Just because the explanation tried to eat something bigger than its head doesn't really make it an accomplishment in piecing together a scattered whole; it just failed in a more verbose fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One can easily flip it around and go with the standard WtA cosmology as being the end all be all. Demon can fit in it rather easy. It just takes a bit of plotting. </div> </div> </div>Most notably by demons being unreliable due to being stuck outside of all realities for a long measure of time and fused with human vessels. Their memories were always meant to be rather sketchy; the combination of that and whatever scraps of faith they latched onto in their human body makes for a rather unsettled and tattered view of the cosmos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T17:27:13-07:00","id":1206201,"title":"","content":"Just because you don't like something doesn't make it a failure. Demon does a fairly good job connecting the dots. Maybe some don't like how they did it, but it wasn't exactly an easy job either.<br /> <br /> It's funny. I can remember years ago how much Vampire-centric players hated WtA cosmology for telling them what's what. Players are perfectly fine with the WtA line hyper-explaining their world view as canon and all the other splats are swimming in ignorance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","name":"thespiraleffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T18:01:28-07:00","id":1206208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thespiraleffect</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1206201#post1206201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you don't like something doesn't make it a failure. Demon does a fairly good job connecting the dots. Maybe some don't like how they did it, but it wasn't exactly an easy job either.</div> </div> </div> </div>There weren't any dots to connect in the first place; any picture that you end up with is going to require a lot of your own work to draw, with no particular framework or help given on what the end product is supposed to look like. You don't get much from playing the &quot;you can't comprehend the true shape&quot; card and then trying to explain said true shape.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's funny. I can remember years ago how much Vampire-centric players hated WtA cosmology for telling them what's what. Players are perfectly fine with the WtA line hyper-explaining their world view as canon and all the other splats are swimming in ignorance. </div> </div> </div>W:tA doesn't offer nearly so many words to qualify as &quot;hyper-explaining&quot;; the hierarchy of spirits is extremely loose, the concept of &quot;this is the soul of the world&quot; is not exactly complicated, even when you get into how the world broke. The Umbra was custom-made for Werewolf, and its various regions are great with a self-contained setup that explains its own basic conceit. Other games didn't have to try and piggyback on this, and quite frankly, shouldn't have; it wasn't a setup made to support their themes from the ground up, and really didn't need to end up complicated by their inclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 04-12-2018, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T20:58:05-07:00","id":1206262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1206116#post1206116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the Author who wrote the Demon section explained he never intended the Wraith Charon to be the Demon, only to inherit the name as a sort of title. Nhudri on the other hand seems to be Nhudriel.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said - he's never explained as one of the Fallen, it's a misreading of the text that gives people the idea that he was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T21:50:00-07:00","id":1206273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1206262#post1206262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I said - he's never explained as one of the Fallen, it's a misreading of the text that gives people the idea that he was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not a misreading, but more people just jumping to conclusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T04:44:40-07:00","id":1207218,"title":"","content":"As much as I would love to see H20, I doubt we'll see any more 20 stuff just to avoid market confusion. WW is going to want to keep everything in the new system and push that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T05:39:58-07:00","id":1207226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1207218#post1207218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I would love to see H20, I doubt we'll see any more 20 stuff just to avoid market confusion. WW is going to want to keep everything in the new system and push that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be my guess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T13:52:59-07:00","id":1207399,"title":"","content":"To be fair I don't need Hunter as much as the other stuff, since I feel the Corebook is still just as relevant. I feel Hunter Books were mostly fluff for canon and not pertinent to actually running a hunter game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T14:42:04-07:00","id":1209015,"title":"","content":"Plus you get the Hunter Hunted 2 book. It's not a core book but it does give you guidelines and set up for creating a Hunter type character in the 20th Anniversary setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23951-acwrig2","name":"acwrig2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T05:58:38-07:00","id":1212241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acwrig2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1209015#post1209015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus you get the Hunter Hunted 2 book. It's not a core book but it does give you guidelines and set up for creating a Hunter type character in the 20th Anniversary setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I've always found hunters and Hunters to be a weird thing within the WoD.<br /> <br /> &quot;You see, a Vampire almost killed me, and it woke something within me-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, you Awakened? You're a Magus!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, no, you see in that moment I made the choice to fight back, to be the light in the darkness-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, a faithful hunter, I understand.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No you see I was chosen by a higher power to defend against dark forces-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mummy? No, wait, you're talking about your First Change? You're a Werewolf!&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean everyone has their own limits when it comes to Kitchen Sink effect. For me, personally, Hunters (as in the Imbued Hunters) feel like a strange addition. Hunters Hunted already has options ranging from normal mortals fighting the supernatural (which is the core appeal of being a &quot;Hunter&quot; for many), all the way up to mortals with numina as an edge (another idea, the &quot;Buffy&quot; style hunter, which is a common aspiration for people who want to play as a Hunter). The existence of the Imbued feels like a strange thing to add on top; there's a reason that Hungry Dead, Fera, Demons, Fomori and Mummies get references across the books, whereas references to the Imbued are relatively sparse. The only one I remember is a small section saying that Dhampir can't become Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:06:39-07:00","id":1212284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1212241#post1212241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, personally, Hunters (as in the Imbued Hunters) feel like a strange addition. Hunters Hunted already has options ranging from normal mortals fighting the supernatural (which is the core appeal of being a &quot;Hunter&quot; for many), all the way up to mortals with numina as an edge (another idea, the &quot;Buffy&quot; style hunter, which is a common aspiration for people who want to play as a Hunter). The existence of the Imbued feels like a strange thing to add on top; there's a reason that Hungry Dead, Fera, Demons, Fomori and Mummies get references across the books, whereas references to the Imbued are relatively sparse. The only one I remember is a small section saying that Dhampir can't become Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Capital-H Hunters are kind of a temporary thing in a way, if you think about it.<br /> Originally in the Metaplot, the first Hunters gained their powers and received their messages just after the Avatar Storm broke out, the Underworld got ravaged from the explosions during the Week of Nightmares, the living dead began spewing from their graves in accelerated numbers, and the Abyss cracked open. (I.e. switch from 2nd to Revised)<br /> <br /> Essentially, at least Metaplot-wise, there is a certain quite good premise for some humans to suddenly be imbued by observing higher powers. And then the Metaplot kind of drove towards its conclusion in the Apocalypse/Gehenna/Ascension etc.<br /> <br /> Given that the Metaplot will now continue into the present days, with no cataclysm rocking the world anymore, then I can see a metaplot reason for the Hunters to actually slowly dwindle in numbers again, with no new imbued filling the gaps left by those that die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:09:17-07:00","id":1212366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1212241#post1212241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existence of the Imbued feels like a strange thing to add on top; there's a reason that Hungry Dead, Fera, Demons, Fomori and Mummies get references across the books, whereas references to the Imbued are relatively sparse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that the reason you don't see a ton of references to the Imbued, as opposed to other splats, is because Reckoning came out at a time when White Wolf was diminishing their output of books .Werewolf, Mage, Vampire, etc. had 5 plus years of material out there to reference each other. Hunter the Reckoning did not. And there were still plenty of references of the Imbued in a number of books.<br /> <br /> I don't think Hunters had less references than Demons, Kindred of the East, or Mummies. But hey, if that's a statistical analysis you're stating, then I guess it's true. I just don't FEEL it's true, but I'd have to check the books. <br /> <br /> Hunter was supposed to be self-contained. It worked better that way, IMO.<br /> <br /> Edit: And Ambrosia has some great points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 04-27-2018, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:50:51-07:00","id":1212373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1212241#post1212241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existence of the Imbued feels like a strange thing to add on top; there's a reason that Hungry Dead, Fera, Demons, Fomori and Mummies get references across the books, whereas references to the Imbued are relatively sparse.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Hungry Dead, Fera, Fomori, and Mummies had a lot longer runs in the World of Darkness than you're giving them credit. Mummies had a first/second edition book like Hunters Hunted well before Resurrection was a thing. Fomori were at latest a second edition foe for Garou. Even the other Fera had vague mentions in the Werewolf series before they were player available, as I'm fairly positive both Rage Across the Amazon and Rage Across Australia predated the Changing Breed books. Even the beginnings of the Hungry Dead - designed as Kindred, no less - were in A World of Darkness (Gaki bloodline) and Dark Alliance: Vancouver (Bushi Bloodline), both of which are somewhere around the first/second edition change, as well, if I recall the timing correctly. Only Demons, as in the Fallen, came truly late to the party with capital H Hunters, since it's unlikely that the demons that infernalists do &quot;business&quot; with are capital D Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:14:14-07:00","id":1212379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1212284#post1212284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Capital-H Hunters are kind of a temporary thing in a way, if you think about it.<br /> Originally in the Metaplot, the first Hunters gained their powers and received their messages just after the Avatar Storm broke out, the Underworld got ravaged from the explosions during the Week of Nightmares, the living dead began spewing from their graves in accelerated numbers, and the Abyss cracked open. (I.e. switch from 2nd to Revised)<br /> <br /> Essentially, at least Metaplot-wise, there is a certain quite good premise for some humans to suddenly be imbued by observing higher powers. And then the Metaplot kind of drove towards its conclusion in the Apocalypse/Gehenna/Ascension etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Dark Ages Revised-era Inquisitors acting as a deliberate prequel to Imbued Hunters? They're mechanically similar, and even make sense in their differences as a metaplot &quot;alpha test&quot; of the Imbued. I won't go so far as to claim that, like the Imbued, Inquisitors would be revealed as receiving their power from Lucifer or something, but I'll definitely say that White Wolf gave us a genuine retcon by making Leopold von Murnau an Inquisitor. That establishes every metaplot point involving the Society of Leopold as historically attached to what were essentially the Dark Medieval Imbued. That's not nothing, and it most certainly isn't a &quot;temporary thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm not sure how everyone else has handled or would handle this information. Some may integrate it into a larger Reckoning scenario while others might wave it away as regular hunters with Numina. However it's played, though, we've got solid, canonical metaplot tying a (H)unter splat directly to a (h)unter organization large enough to be a common threat to the supernatural. It's an issue to be dealt with, one way or another","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":".  Typos 04-27-2018, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:26:58-07:00","id":1212384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1212379#post1212379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, I'm not sure how everyone else has or would handle this information. Some may integrate it into a larger Reckoning scenario while others might wave it away as regular hunters with Numina. However it's played, though, we've got solid, canonical metaplot tying a (H)unter splat directly to a (h)unter organization large enough to be common threat to the supernatural. It's an issue to be dealt with, one way or another</div> </div> </div> </div>Or be swept under the rug, really.<br /> I kind of hope that the 'Second Inquisition' that NuWW has hinted at for their V5 Metaplot changes directly involves *something* along those lines. Not on a large scale, at least on the paranormal humans front - too many imbued/hunters with Numina would change the flair of WoD a bit too much - but it would be a good way to work it in. Keep the hunters a bit more mysterious, even, than the Monsters themselves. That would be a very typical WoD twist.<br /> <br /> However, if the Second Inquisition won't involve any of that, then it's kind of up for grabs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T12:38:24-07:00","id":1213148,"title":"","content":"I'm hopeful that the 2nd Inquisition will focus on **all** supernatural beings, and not just on vampires. I'm also hopeful that the final version of 5th Edition will actually use blood pools, won't make Disciplines entirely dependent upon what kind of human you're eating, and that they'll de-LARP the Disciplines and give us something closer to what V20 had. <br /> <br /> With regard to My supposedly misreading the bit about Charon, or &quot;making assumptions&quot;, no. Developer chats AFTER THE FACT change nothing. When I was reading in the book, Charon was said to be a demon, with NO mention of another Charon, who was a Wraith. I'm not calling the developer a liar, but I am saying that it's not misreading or making assumptions when you look at what text says in a book and take it at face value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T14:16:13-07:00","id":1213184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1198181#post1198181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I will be disappointed if we don't get Kindred of the East, Mummy, and Demon! And to a lesser extent hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred of the east is frickin' underrated, at least here in italy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My English sucks. Sorry.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23549-toreadorgentleman","name":"ToreadorGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T15:05:27-07:00","id":1213192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1213148#post1213148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hopeful that the 2nd Inquisition will focus on **all** supernatural beings, and not just on vampires. I'm also hopeful that the final version of 5th Edition will actually use blood pools, won't make Disciplines entirely dependent upon what kind of human you're eating, and that they'll de-LARP the Disciplines and give us something closer to what V20 had.<br /> <br /> With regard to My supposedly misreading the bit about Charon, or &quot;making assumptions&quot;, no. Developer chats AFTER THE FACT change nothing. When I was reading in the book, Charon was said to be a demon, with NO mention of another Charon, who was a Wraith. I'm not calling the developer a liar, but I am saying that it's not misreading or making assumptions when you look at what text says in a book and take it at face value.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ...what do you mean Developer clarification doesn't matter that is silly.<br /> <br /> And the Demon Book talks about super ancient Prehistory... you know before the Wraith Charon was even born much less died, so there was only one Charon then. And you can't just say no as a counter argument, that is laughably nonsensical. Demon gives the story of the First Charon, they also leave a lot of mystery. And that is it. It would also make very little sense if Charon in Wraith was the original Demon Charon, I mean he has a Pasiphae for Godsake, and he looked to the Lady of Fate, Eve, as more a mentor which would be weird for Demon Charon unless he suffers from lots of Amnesia. And Charon seems more to display Wraith Powers rather then Demon Lores.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T09:36:03-07:00","id":1213464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1198170-demon-the-fallen-mummy-20th-anniversary-edition?p=1213148#post1213148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hopeful that the 2nd Inquisition will focus on **all** supernatural beings, and not just on vampires. I'm also hopeful that the final version of 5th Edition will actually use blood pools, won't make Disciplines entirely dependent upon what kind of human you're eating, and that they'll de-LARP the Disciplines and give us something closer to what V20 had.<br /> <br /> With regard to My supposedly misreading the bit about Charon, or &quot;making assumptions&quot;, no. Developer chats AFTER THE FACT change nothing. When I was reading in the book, Charon was said to be a demon, with NO mention of another Charon, who was a Wraith. I'm not calling the developer a liar, but I am saying that it's not misreading or making assumptions when you look at what text says in a book and take it at face value.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two beings can share names. How did you manage to ignore the very well attested origins of Charon was a mortal man of Mycenae to make that leap? Did you also decide that the Promethean movement was a bunch of mage-familiars, that Prince Balthazar and Thomas Ewell were the same person, or that the Lamia ghoul Lilith was the same as the One and Only Dark Mother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}